$ nexoctl dist ls mem
No distribution.

$ nexoctl dist create mem site --bucket web --prefix /prod --domain www.example.com --domain example.com --index index.html --spa /index.html --comment the web site
Created the distribution `site` (website) of `web/prod` on www.example.com, example.com.

$ nexoctl dist create mem api --bucket data --mode s3 --domain s3.example.com --access authenticated
Created the distribution `api` (s3) of `data` on s3.example.com.

$ nexoctl dist create mem clash --bucket web --domain example.com
! nexoctl: error: distribution "clash": example.com: alias already used by another distribution (alias_conflict)
[exit 1]

$ nexoctl dist create mem nobucket --domain x.example.com
! nexoctl: error: --bucket is required
! Run 'nexoctl dist create --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl dist ls mem
ID                   STATE    MODE     ORIGIN               TLS                DOMAINS
api                  enabled  s3       data                 -                  s3.example.com
site                 enabled  website  web/prod             -                  www.example.com, example.com

$ nexoctl dist info mem site
ID: site
State: enabled
Mode: website
Origin: web/prod
Domains: www.example.com, example.com
Default behavior: access public, index index.html, spa /index.html
Comment: the web site
TLS: -

$ nexoctl dist info mem nope
! nexoctl: error: distribution "nope": distribution not found: nope (distribution_not_found)
[exit 3]

$ nexoctl dist resolve mem example.com
example.com: distribution `site` (alias example.com, website), bucket web

$ nexoctl dist resolve mem unknown.example.org
unknown.example.org: path-style

$ nexoctl dist domain add mem site *.preview.example.com
Domains of `site`: www.example.com, example.com, *.preview.example.com.

$ nexoctl dist domain remove mem site *.preview.example.com
Domains of `site`: www.example.com, example.com.

$ nexoctl dist behavior add mem site --prefix /assets/ --cache-control public, max-age=31536000, immutable
Added a behavior for prefix /assets/ to `site` (1 behavior).

$ nexoctl dist keygroup create mem downloads --comment download links
Created the key group `downloads` with the key KMEM0006 (ed25519); private key saved to $WORK/.nexoctl/keys/mem/KMEM0006.pem.

$ nexoctl dist keygroup ls mem
downloads (1 key)
  KMEM0006 ed25519 2026-01-02 03:04:05 UTC [private key stored]

$ nexoctl dist behavior add mem site --glob /downloads/** --access signed --key-group downloads
Added a behavior for glob /downloads/** to `site` (2 behaviors).

$ nexoctl dist behavior ls mem site
1. prefix /assets/ → cache-control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
2. glob /downloads/** → access signed, key group downloads
default → access public, index index.html, spa /index.html

$ nexoctl dist behavior move mem site 2 1
Moved the behavior 2 of `site` to position 1.

$ nexoctl dist behavior ls mem site
1. glob /downloads/** → access signed, key group downloads
2. prefix /assets/ → cache-control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
default → access public, index index.html, spa /index.html

$ nexoctl dist error-page set mem site 404 /404.html
Errors 404 of `site` answer /404.html.

$ nexoctl dist redirect add mem site --from ^/old/(.*)$ --to /new/$1 --status 308
Added the redirection 1 of `site`: ^/old/(.*)$ → /new/$1 (308).

$ nexoctl dist headers mem site --security --set X-Site: prod --cors-origin https://app.example.com
Updated the headers of `site` (5 response headers).

$ nexoctl dist restrict mem site --deny-ip 203.0.113.0/24
Updated the restrictions of `site`.

$ nexoctl dist test mem site /downloads/v1.zip
Route: www.example.com → distribution `site` (alias www.example.com)
Behavior: 1 (glob /downloads/**)
Access: signed
Settings: access signed, key group downloads, index index.html, spa /index.html
